 {"id":"fabro-645d","title":"Implementer prompt: scoped reads via sed -n when the brief pins line anchors","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:10:29.468Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:48:00.284Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md` (shell guidance), add: when the brief names line anchors, read with `sed -n '<range>p'` instead of whole-file `cat`. Evidence from run 01M1YY8JJCE31XHSDCZ816634G: the implementer ran `cat -n` over the entire 111-line `planner.md` (12,096 bytes, event seq 84–85) although the brief pinned the targets ('step 3, line ~35', table ~line 28) and the edit itself used exact-string replace. Expected effect: ~10 KB less context per platform-file edit pass. Reviewer-side analog fabro-9a43 exists; no seed covers the implementer prompt's read discipline — new mechanism on a different node. Basis: run 01M1YY8JJCE31XHSDCZ816634G, workflow version 08846dfb574d2ff5db4e16cc712b4a81c7801307975d397a365a9bc676a3d611, commit e53f85be88b2b379a31ff2822a7eb564e9637fda","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-06e0","title":"develop planner: in-flight PR guard is credential-less and must STAY that way — use fabro_runs_list, remove gh from the toolchain image","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:06:56.713Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:33:12.602Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"USER DECISIONS 2026-09-08: (D1) Weg A ONLY - extend existing surfaces, NO new tools; (D2) gh REMOVED from the toolchain image by direct revert (commit f00fdb102, capability change without user decision gets reverted per ADR-0019) - image rebuilt and verified (gh absent, sd/rg/just/nu + mise trust intact). SECURITY CONTEXT: the engine injects GITHUB_TOKEN + a git credential bridge into agent shell calls - so the brief gh presence was a write-capable forge client in agent shells, NOT a harmless unauthenticated binary as first assumed; the prohibition rationale is documented on fabro-05d0 and ADR-0019.\n\nREMAINING WORK (this seed): (1) check the OpenAPI/runs list projection - if it lacks pull_request {number, state}, extend it (read-only data enrichment of the existing engine-mediated response); (2) planner guard (.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 4 IN-FLIGHT PR CHECK): replace the gh command with fabro_runs_list -> filter runs with open/non-terminal linked PR -> extract seed ids from run goals -> skip matching candidates, journal 'skipped: in-flight PR <n>', continue down sd ready --assignee fabro; remove the gh fail-open clause (no gh exists anymore - the guard must not reference it). Acceptance: a develop pass with a seed whose PR sits open in the gate journals 'skipped: in-flight PR <n>' and claims a DIFFERENT seed - verified live; planner prompt no longer mentions gh; no credential added; no new agent tool exists.","labels":["workflows","revision","engine"]}
 {"id":"fabro-16ff","title":"revisor + reviewer must become security-affine (ADR-0019): capability-affecting ideas get shot down at filing and review time","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:23:10.858Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:33:18.994Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"USER DIRECTIVE 2026-09-08: 'der revisor und der reviewer muessen unbedingt sicherheits-affiner werden, sodass solche ideen von vornherein abgeschmettert werden' - the gh incident (PR #53 baked a forge client into the toolchain image; a follow-up seed proposed GH_TOKEN provisioning) only stayed harmless because credentials happen to be absent from sandboxes - luck, not design. The two autonomous gates must enforce ADR-0019 themselves.\n\nFIX (1) REVISOR file stage (.fabro/workflows/revisor/prompts/file.md): add to the seed-intake rules - when a finding or proposed fix direction would ADD/CHANGE/REMOVE a tool, credential, or permission in an agent-reachable surface (Dockerfiles, environment env, tool allowlists, hook configs, new binaries): (a) the seed MUST carry labels needs-user (in addition to revision) and stay for user assignment per ADR-0018 D3; (b) the seed body must cite ADR-0019 and state 'implementation awaits explicit user approval'; (c) the revisor NEVER proposes raw authenticated clients or token provisioning as fix directions - engine-mediated, read-only, extend-existing-tools is the only vocabulary (ADR-0019.2/.3).\nFIX (2) DEVELOP reviewer (.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md): add a review axis to the checklist - CAPABILITY DELTA: if the diff touches .fabro/Dockerfile*, env/credential provisioning, tool allowlists, hook configs, or adds binaries/secrets to agent surfaces, verify the seed records an explicit user decision (ADR-0019 citation + approval note); without it, that is a BLOCKING finding -> route Changes requested naming ADR-0019 (a merged capability change without user decision gets reverted). Capability REDUCTIONS (removing tools/credentials, least-privilege narrowing) are fine and welcome - do not block those, just verify they cite their basis.\nAcceptance: revisor files a capability-affecting seed with needs-user + ADR-0019 citation (verifiable on the next such finding); reviewer prompt carries the capability axis; one gate run demonstrates a blocking Changes-requested on a capability delta without recorded approval (test or staged verification).\n\nADDITIONAL EVIDENCE (2026-09-08): the gh incident was WORSE than first diagnosed - the engine injects GITHUB_TOKEN into every agent shell call (resolve_workflow_env) plus a git credential bridge (git_bridge.rs), so the baked gh was fully WRITE-CAPABLE (merge/close/force-push/branch-delete), not a harmless unauthenticated binary. The reviewers approved PR #53 partly because the per-tool-call env injection was invisible from a container-env perspective. The capability axis must teach reviewers to check what the ENGINE hands to agent shells (env injection, credential bridges), not just what the diff itself adds.","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
-{"id":"fabro-cf76","title":"Planner: verify spec-named headings/anchors/paths exist in target files before forwarding the brief","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:43:30.656Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:48:00.414Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md` step 7 (contradiction check), add: when the spec names a heading/anchor/path, confirm it exists in the target file; when it doesn't, annotate the actual location in the brief. Evidence: the run brief forwarded 'checklist gains a CAPABILITY DELTA axis' verbatim, but `reviewer.md` has no heading named 'checklist' (the numbered 'Your job this pass' list is it); the implementer burned a ~14 s / 519-reasoning-token block deciding placement (events seq 95-97). Expected effect: shorter implementer passes and fewer misplacement deviations → fewer Changes-requested cycles (~2.5 min + ~$0.15 each).\nBasis: run 01M1Z017EQK3Q2QCEMTA6XXNSK, workflow version 78ff76ac6dc73632d1cb65e7e2667edcf4d8b52bf90c47667776f8195ee52e5f, commit 91e7b67f7ec6a4f9470dc082882f4cd9fc59b59f","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
