 {"id":"fabro-eed2","title":"Reviewer prompt: document the == evidence complete == terminal marker in the blob-ref paragraph","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:43:36.726Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:48:00.563Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md` (blob-ref paragraph), add one sentence: the capture ends with `== evidence complete ==` (printed by `scripts/evidence.nu:431`); seeing it means the diff was not cut. Evidence: this run's reviewer journaled that this marker 'was the deciding signal' for completeness but only discovered it after paging to the end of the blob. Expected effect: reviewers approve from a single confident paged read instead of reading to EOF or risking Verification-blocked re-capture (~40 s). Complements fabro-a0fe (how to page) and fabro-8d2c (avoid the blob detour) without overlapping their mechanisms.\nBasis: run 01M1Z017EQK3Q2QCEMTA6XXNSK, workflow version 78ff76ac6dc73632d1cb65e7e2667edcf4d8b52bf90c47667776f8195ee52e5f, commit 91e7b67f7ec6a4f9470dc082882f4cd9fc59b59f","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-e505","title":"engine: honor run.integrations.github token grants ONLY for User-principal runs — agent-authored config must never mint credentials (ADR-0019.6)","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":0,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:44:13.872Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:50:21.132Z","assignee":"agent","description":"ESCALATION CHAIN (user analysis 2026-09-08): the line's agents WRITE their own workflow configs (.fabro/workflows/** via PRs - the revision seed class does exactly this, see PRs #45/#49/#55) - so an agent (or a compromised one) could add [run.integrations.github] permissions to any workflow and the engine would mint a fully write-capable GITHUB_TOKEN into its own sandbox env (resolve_workflow_env is opt-in BY CONFIG ONLY). Combined with exfiltration channels (shell curl, web_fetch) this is deliberate self-escalation + token leak. The config possibility itself must go (ADR-0019.6: the sandbox stays credential-free, repo-contents access only).\n\nFIX: the Principal enum (fabro-types principal.rs: User/Worker/Webhook/Slack/System) already distinguishes run creators. Gate the token path on it: in initialize.rs where spec.github_integration.is_token_requested() is checked, ONLY honor the request when the run was created by a User principal; for Worker/System/Webhook/Slack principals take the no_token path unconditionally (empty env, no bridge), and log/admit a warning naming ADR-0019.6 when a non-user run's config requested permissions (visible signal, silent no-token for the sandbox). Admission-side (server run-create for worker principals): consider rejecting specs whose workflow declares github permissions with a clear error naming ADR-0019 - evaluate which layer gives the clearer failure (recommendation: initialize-side no_token + server-side admission warning; hard rejection if cheap).\nAcceptance: a Worker-principal run whose workflow.toml declares permissions gets NO GITHUB_TOKEN in any shell env and no credential bridge (wire test); a User-principal run (code-review) still gets its scoped token (existing tests stay green); a warning is observable when the config requested it. Current line configs are already tokenless (dd5cd294c) - this closes the REGRANT hole.","labels":["engine"]}
 {"id":"fabro-0f22","title":"engine: scrub clone token from sandbox remote URL — engine git ops switch to transient per-exec credentials (user decision 2026-09-08)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:44:13.979Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:50:21.231Z","description":"USER DECISION 2026-09-08: 'das clone token darf auch nicht zur verfuegung stehen, die remote url wird nach dem clonen nicht gebraucht und ist eine tickende zeitbombe' - option (a) chosen: credential-free sandbox, repo-contents access only (ADR-0019.6).\n\nCURRENT STATE: docker.rs/daytona clone embeds the minted token in the remote origin URL (embed_token_in_url); push_credentials.rs drives engine pushes through EXACTLY that embedded token (compare -> set-url -> record, with re-embed drift recovery at sandbox.rs:1994-1998; daytona rewrites set-url on refresh). Any agent can read it via 'git remote get-url origin' and exfiltrate via curl/web_fetch.\n\nDESIGN (decided): (1) after clone+checkout completes, scrub the remote to the CLEAN https URL ('git remote set-url origin https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>') - the token never persists in repo config; (2) ALL engine-side git network ops (branch push, fetch/refresh, drift recovery) switch to TRANSIENT per-exec credentials: docker_exec_shell already accepts env_vars - pass a GIT_CONFIG overlay (GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/GIT_CONFIG_KEY_x=http.<origin>.extraheader with the basic-auth header) exactly like git_bridge.rs merge_git_bridge_env already builds for shells; the credential exists only in that exec's env, never in repo config, never in agent tool env; (3) the re-embed drift path becomes re-MINT + transient exec instead of set-url; (4) agent-side fetch/pull to origin degrade (they should not need network git - engine does all forge ops); document that in the iterate/agent guidance if a prompt references git pull.\n\nAcceptance: 'git remote get-url origin' in a fresh run container shows the CLEAN url (no token anywhere in config: grep -r x-access-token .git -> empty); engine push/refresh still work (run PRs merge as before, live-verified on the next line pass); no credential reachable from any agent shell or journal; wire tests for push+scrub+transient-exec.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"assignee":"agent"}
